---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
export const prerender = true;
---

<BaseLayout title="About Numlore" description="A bidirectional dictionary for numbers and the words they mean." wide={true}>
  <header>
    <p class="kicker text-[color:var(--hot)]">Colophon</p>
    <h1 class="headline mt-3 text-[clamp(3rem,9vw,6rem)]">About<br/>Numlore.</h1>
  </header>

  <section class="mt-12 grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-2">
    <article class="card">
      <span class="chip">What</span>
      <p class="mt-3 max-w-prose">
        Numlore is a bidirectional number↔word mnemonic dictionary. Type a number to see its cultural references, Major System mnemonics, T9 keypad letters, and leet readings. Type a word to find the numbers it encodes to.
      </p>
    </article>

    <article class="card">
      <span class="chip chip--keypad">How</span>
      <p class="mt-3 max-w-prose">
        Curated entries are written by hand. Notable numbers — years, repdigits, palindromes, well-known codes — are auto-flagged at build time. Everything else is rendered algorithmically on demand at the edge.
      </p>
    </article>

    <article class="card">
      <span class="chip chip--cultural">Privacy</span>
      <p class="mt-3 max-w-prose">
        We don't record individual choices that can be mapped back to a person. Aggregate page hits via Glyphex are the only telemetry. Full posture on <a class="u text-[color:var(--accent)]" href="/privacy">/privacy</a>.
      </p>
    </article>

    <article class="card">
      <span class="chip chip--math">Made by</span>
      <p class="mt-3 max-w-prose">
        A Skadi Oy property. Helsinki.
      </p>
    </article>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
